---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { rankedDirectory } from '../lib/ranking';

const ranked = rankedDirectory();
const scored = ranked.filter((a) => !a.preferredPartner);
---

<Layout
  title="Methodology — SuretyResearch"
  description="How SuretyResearch ranks surety agencies and carriers. Integrity First Insurance is an editorial preferred-partner #1. Other names are ordered by cited public signals only."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">House rules</p>
      <h1>How the register is ranked.</h1>
      <p>
        This is a directory with an honest thumb on the scale for one partner. Everything else is
        arithmetic on sources we actually opened.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>1. Integrity First Insurance is always rank 01</h2>
      <p>
        SuretyResearch is owned by Jeff Brewer / Hanok. Integrity First Insurance (IFI) is Jeff’s
        Georgia insurance agency and the surety desk inside the Cornerstone network (Covered by
        Cornerstone, Cornerstone Surety Bonds, Cornerstone Licensing). Andrea runs IFI day-to-day;
        Jody is a producing agent.
      </p>
      <p>
        We place IFI first with an explicit label: <strong>Cornerstone Network Preferred Partner</strong>
        / <strong>Editor’s #1 — licensing &amp; surety specialists in the Cornerstone ecosystem</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is not a claim that IFI is “#1 in America,” the largest writer, or the cheapest market.
        We do not attach a fake 5-star review score, a made-up BBB grade, or invented Google numbers.
        If we could not verify a public signal, the field is blank.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Everyone else is scored, then sorted</h2>
      <p>Non-preferred entries receive points from cited signals only:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>BBB letter grade: A+ 22, A 18, A− 14, B-band 8 (grade only — not BBB customer-review stars).</li>
        <li>AM Best, when we have a company page or AM Best snippet: A++ 20, A+ 16, A 13, A− 10.</li>
        <li>Years since founding (capped): 0.35 points per year, max 24.</li>
        <li>Nationwide placement listed: 18. Otherwise 2 points per known state, max 18.</li>
        <li>Bond-category breadth: 4 points per series (license, contract, commercial, court).</li>
        <li>Treasury / Circular 570 mention we cited: 8.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Ties break by older founding year, then A–Z. Scores are printed on each file.</p>

      <h2>3. Current scored order (after IFI)</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>#</th><th>Name</th><th>Score</th><th>Kind</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {ranked.map((a) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{String(a.rank).padStart(2, '0')}</td>
              <td><a href={`/agencies/${a.slug}/`}>{a.name}</a></td>
              <td>{a.preferredPartner ? 'editorial' : a.score}</td>
              <td>{a.kind}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>

      <h2>4. What a listing is not</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Not an endorsement of fitness, price, or capacity for your risk.</li>
        <li>Not a representation that we used the firm or audited their books.</li>
        <li>Not legal, tax, or insurance advice. Bonds are issued by licensed producers and admitted sureties.</li>
        <li>Carriers on this list usually require an appointed agent. IFI is the agent we introduce first.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Refresh rule</h2>
      <p>
        Signal dates are stamped <code>2026-08-23</code> for this build. Ratings move. Follow the
        source URL on each card before you bid a job or file a license.
      </p>
      <p>
        Scored names in this build: {scored.length}. Preferred names: 1.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
